 "about": "Real MacBook trackpad wheel recordings (Firefox 156, macOS) curated from the owner's carousel-overscroll bench telemetry (sessions recorded 2026-09-28 on bench rev 33-40), plus two clearly-marked SYNTHETIC recordings. Replayed by playwright/wheel-replay.ts.",
 "timing": "The telemetry has NO per-event timestamps: each burst stores only its ordered deltas (first 80), its event count and one total duration `ms` (first event to the moment the NEXT gesture began, so it includes any trailing silence). Events are therefore spaced UNIFORMLY at `intervalMs` = ms/events where that is consistent with a 60Hz stream (<= 20ms, or the burst was ended by a re-push so there is no trailing silence); otherwise 17ms is used (the median ms/events of the 17 re-push-ended bursts is 17.8ms; Firefox delivers wheel events once per frame). Real inter-event jitter is lost. `t` = ms since the first event.",
 "sign": "dx < 0 at the start edge and dx > 0 at the end edge (bench convention: cd = -d). Real recordings store the single signed delta the bench used (deltaX if non-zero else deltaY); it is replayed as dx with dy 0, the horizontal two-finger swipe a trackpad sends. deltaMode is 0 (pixels) for all real data.",
 "fields": "arrivalIndex: (native kinds) event index at which the browser's own momentum scroll is assumed to reach the edge; the real index was not recorded, so it is a documented approximation. repushIndex: index of the first event of the dip-then-rise re-push. edge: the edge the recording pushes toward. recorded: what the bench itself logged for the source burst.",
